Fictional EP Tracklist

Track 1: Cicadas Drink the Sawdust
- Story & Context: Recorded during the chaotic final hour of the Black Mountain wedding reception, the track documents the exact moment the Drossel family's generator began spitting blue fire into the center ring while an unseasonal October frost chilled the air. Elihu Vane slammed his banjo neck into an amplifier cabinet, triggering a wild, 150-BPM clawhammer brawl against Mercy’s screeching synthesizer organ patches as drunken aerialists hurled broken champagne flutes into the ring. Above the screaming crowd and the smell of ozone and wet canvas, the two dynasties locked eyes and wailed together: "Drink the brine, spill the cake, the brood will fly before we wake."
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: High-contrast 1990s flash photography of an overturned multi-tiered wedding cake smashed into blood-red circus sawdust, covered in swarming golden cicadas, surrounded by broken fiddle bows and glowing vacuum tubes in the dim gloom of a canvas tent.

Track 2: Lydia Sheds Her Carapace
- Story & Context: Written in an unheated trailer behind the menagerie cages, this confession piece centers on Lydia Vane, the runaway bride who spent the entire wedding feast scraping greasepaint and silk skin off her bleeding arms in a porcelain basin of melted ice. Mercy Drossel tracked the sorrowful tune on a solitary Roland JD-800 digital glass pad, underlaid only by Elihu’s skeletal, gut-string banjo picked with silver thimbles that rattled against the headstock. Her voice cracked through a dead bullhorn as she admitted her plan to poison both family heads: "I shed the silk, I shed the wing, I leave you rot inside the ring."
