Track 3: “Did the Mantis Catch the Trapeze?”
- Story & Context: The final aftermath cut preserves the local legend of the fire that consumed the wedding pavilion at dawn, where elderly knife-thrower Silas Drossel allegedly saw an immense winged apparition swinging through the burning rigging ropes above the panic. The track fuses real mountain fiddle cries with a suffocating, degraded digital synth choir that stutters erratically, punctuated by the metallic clank of falling tent poles and church bells recorded through a walkie-talkie. A chilling, unamplified field recording captures the surviving family singing the hook over the embers: "Hold the pitch, drop the shroud, the sky has eaten up the crowd."
